{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1241,1347p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | nl -ba -v 1241\"","aggregated_output":"  1241\t\n  1242\t| `:yin.k/status` | Raised by | Carries |\n  1243\t|---|---|---|\n  1244\t| `:yin.k/ok` | any | the value, or the lowered VM |\n  1245\t| `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` | lift | `:yin.k/segment`, `:yin.k/pc` |\n  1246\t| `:yin.k/not-quiescent` | lift | the ready-queue depth |\n  1247\t| `:yin.k/non-portable` | lift | `:yin.k/path`, `:yin.k/kind`, `:yin.k/hint` — kinds at §7.5.4, cycles included as `:kind :cyclic` |\n  1248\t| `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` | lower | `:yin.k/contract` expected and found |\n  1249\t| `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` | lower | the address claimed and the address computed |\n  1250\t| `:yin.k/undecodable` | lower | `:yin.k/path`, the structural defect — malformed markers, missing or cyclic refs, malformed-but-correctly-hashed bodies |\n  1251\t| `:yin.k/unsatisfied` | lower | `:yin.k/missing`, `:yin.k/discovery` — includes attachment failures, cursor profiles, and an unreachable arbitration medium |\n  1252\t| `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` | lower | `:yin.k/occurrence`, the proposal — a step status while a proposal is unanswered, bounded by nothing (`dao.lease.md`) |\n  1253\t| `:yin.k/not-holder` | lower | `:yin.k/occurrence`, the lease state observed |\n  1254\t\n  1255\tTerminal DaoStream outcomes met during lift or lower (`transport-error`,\n  1256\t`closed`, `invalid-descriptor`, …) are surfaced unchanged inside the UCF\n  1257\toutcome under their own key `:dao.stream/outcome`, exactly as the transport\n  1258\tproduced them; UCF does not rename them, nest them under private keys, or\n  1259\ttranslate between them. FFI requests and responses inside a value use the\n  1260\treference machine's versioned envelope, `dao.stream.apply` —\n  1261\t`:dao.stream.apply/id`, `/op`, `/args`, `/ok`, `/error` — never the\n  1262\tdeleted v1 `dao.stream.apply` vocabulary. Every lower failure names its\n  1263\tcleanup obligation: before custody, none; after custody, release\n  1264\t(§7.8 step 7).\n  1265\t\n  1266\t## §7.10 Invariant compliance\n  1267\t\n  1268\t| Invariant | How UCF honors it |\n  1269\t|---|---|\n  1270\t| No hidden global state | Every dependency is declared in `:yin.k/requires` — *as computed by the declared fixed point, with its completeness stated* (`:yin.k/discovery`); the store travels as an explicit slice restored into an isolated store; fresh-name state and parked records travel explicitly; custody is facts on a named, possessed medium. |\n  1271\t| No implicit control flow | Resume happens only at a safepoint the machine's parking transitions define; the successor chain is explicit `:yin.k/origin` links; the exporting state is an observed data state, never a notification. |\n  1272\t| No callbacks | Lift and lower are step functions; custody is observed, never notified; a lapsed holder stops at its own bound; an unanswered proposal is a step status, not a wait. |\n  1273\t| No shared mutable state | A UCF value is content-addressed and immutable; occurrence identity separates content variants from the one leased computation; two resumers of one value under `:fork` diverge into distinct incarnations; the isolated execution store shares nothing with the resumer's tasks. |\n  1274\t| No layer collapsing | Canonicalize, encode, discover, arbitrate, load, restore, execute are separate functions with data between them. The engine's hot loop is untouched: lifting is a pure function over the blocked machine's value, and the exporting state is that value with an emptied wait-set and a retained record — driver discipline, not engine machinery. |\n  1275\t| No assumed graphs | Sharing is an explicit value table keyed by address; cursor aliasing is an explicit cell graph, not inferred from positions; code refs are pcs relative to an addressed vector; nothing is resolved by pointer; foreign engines reconstruct dynamic state from the frame, never from layouts they assume. |\n  1276\t\n  1277\tAnd the axioms — each claim conditioned on the obligation it depends on: the\n  1278\tcontinuation is a stream value (1); its meaning is supplied by the\n  1279\tresumer's loader and contract stamp, not carried in it (2); its code and its\n  1280\tstate are datoms under `:yin.code/*` and `:yin.k/*` (3); and it pauses,\n  1281\ttravels, and resumes anywhere that **holds what it declares, satisfies the\n  1282\tdeclared cursor profiles, and obtains custody where the policy demands it**\n  1283\t(4) — the unconditional form of that sentence was a claim the unresolved\n  1284\tstate closure, custody enforcement, and effect admission had not earned.\n  1285\t\n  1286\t## §7.11 Acceptance blockers for the implementation phase\n  1287\t\n  1288\tThe warning at the top of this file is retained until each of these is\n  1289\tclosed with a test in the parity or conformance suite. The first four are\n  1290\tthe review's named architectural obligations; they are blockers to\n  1291\t*accepting the design*, not merely work items.\n  1292\t\n  1293\t- **Authority grounding and wiring.** The arbitration `dao.space`, its\n  1294\t  transactor as grantor, the occurrence ledger with epochs, and the\n  1295\t  attribution resolver `dao.lease.md` requires, are composition duties; the\n  1296\t  first composition to ship UCF is `yin.repl.core`'s handoff demo, and\n  1297\t  its wiring becomes the worked example. A composition without a\n  1298\t  transactable space offers `:yin.k/fork` only.\n  1299\t- **Execution identity.** Occurrence minting, the `:yin.k/origin` chain,\n  1300\t  retry idempotence (one occurrence per park), and successor completion as\n  1301\t  a grantor ledger transition need conformance tests, including the crash\n  1302\t  windows of §7.7.5.\n  1303\t- **Pending-state completeness.** Every pending variant of §7.4.3 must\n  1304\t  round-trip and resume *elsewhere*: retained writes, sent and retained FFI\n  1305\t  calls with both endpoints and the kept response cursor, and cursor cells\n  1306\t  through the aliasing scenarios of `check-wait-set`. This depends on a\n  1307\t  **portable cursor profile** in at least one transport, which\n  1308\t  `dao.stream.md` leaves TBD — an external dependency UCF inherits and\n  1309\t  cannot close itself.\n  1310\t- **Enforceable fencing.** Epoch-checked, atomic-with-commitment admission\n  1311\t  and durable op-id dedup at consumers: which consumers check, and how a\n  1312\t  `dao.space` transactor consults the epoch without a callback, is a design\n  1313\t  item for `dao.space.transactor.md`. Until it lands, `:yin.k/exclusive`\n  1314\t  custody is at-least-once and must say so.\n  1315\t- **Canonical byte encoding.** `:yin.code/hash` and `:yin.k/id` are exactly\n  1316\t  as portable as `dao.jing/segment-key`, which is transitional. Closing this\n  1317\t  is `dao.jing`'s open item, not UCF's, but UCF cannot be declared\n  1318\t  cross-host stable before it lands.\n  1319\t- **Contract revision publication.** `:yin.code/contract \"v2\"` needs a\n  1320\t  published revision history naming the complete execution contract\n  1321\t  (§7.3.3): the tuple grammar — mnemonic set, per-mnemonic arity and operand\n  1322\t  kinds, saturation/defaults table — the opcode table and transitions, the\n  1323\t  resolution and last-value-wins rules, the effect outcome map, and the\n  1324\t  scheduler semantics, written into `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.4 beside the\n  1325\t  opcode table.\n  1326\t- **Primitive profile publication.** The standard `yin.vm/primitives`\n  1327\t  map published with profiles (§7.5.2), including the `:effectful`\n  1328\t  declarations for `yin/def` and `require`; reverse-lookup uniqueness\n  1329\t  asserted at `create-vm`.\n  1330\t- **Discovery completeness.** The fixed point of §7.6.1 implemented and\n  1331\t  tested against the `:store-get`/`:store-put`, dynamic-callee, and\n  1332\t  cross-activation-`E` cases; module manifests publishing store footprints\n  1333\t  so `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` disappears.\n  1334\t- **Isolated-store lowering.** Conformance tests that the resumed task's\n  1335\t  store contains exactly the slice and the resumer's pair, and that a\n  1336\t  receiver-side binding of a name in the slice's name set cannot change\n  1337\t  resolution.\n  1338\t- **Safepoint conformance harness.** A test that runs every corpus segment\n  1339\t  on the reference machine to each safepoint of the complete §7.4.1 table —\n  1340\t  effect-producing calls included — lifts, lowers into a fresh VM, and\n  1341\t  checks the parity suite's result; the same harness is what a foreign\n  1342\t  engine runs to claim conformance, including `lift ∘ lower = id`, the\n  1343\t  static `stack-effect`/`lexically-required` checks, and the §7.3.4\n  1344\t  projection/direct-path image-equality assertion.\n  1345\t- **Exporting-state integration.** The lift driver's exporting transition\n  1346\t  and its failure/retry paths, tested specifically against the\n  1347\t  poll-a-blocked-writer-appends hazard of §7.7.4.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
