{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '841,933p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 841\"","aggregated_output":"   841\t```text\n   842\tRenamed:  src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc\n   843\t            -> src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc            (M1)\n   844\t          test/yin/vm/debruijn_linker_test.cljc\n   845\t            -> test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc           (M1)\n   846\tNew:      test/yin/vm/linker_step_test.cljc           (M3)\n   847\t          test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc        (M4)\n   848\tEdited:   src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc                 (M4)\n   849\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc  (:link wait reason)     (M4)\n   850\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/content.cljc (retire load-rows,\n   851\t                                        fetch-vector)          (M2)\n   852\t          src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc                      (M5)\n   853\t          docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n   854\t            (section 7.4.1 row, section 7.4.3 variant)         (M4)\n   855\tDepends:  dao.jing (segment-key, segment-matches?, materialize!)\n   856\t          dao.jing.remote, dao.jing.remote.step, dao.stream.rpc\n   857\t          yin.vm (validate-rows, free-names)\n   858\t          yin.vm.code (well-formed-vector?)\n   859\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n   860\tMust not change:\n   861\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n   862\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing, any kernel's step function\n   863\t```\n   864\t\n   865\t`yin.vm.linker` exports: `fetch`, `verify`, `link-state`, `request-link`,\n   866\t`step`, `abandon`, `publish!`, `ast-format`, `semantic-format`,\n   867\t`stack-format`, `register-format`, `manifest-format`, the four\n   868\tfree-name scanners, `index-from-datoms`, `address-attribute`,\n   869\t`pairing-datoms`, `root-pairing`, `verify-same-root-pairing`,\n   870\t`trusted-fallback`, `verifying-fallback`, `refused`, `refused?`, `ok?`,\n   871\t`refusal-reasons`.\n   872\t\n   873\t## 11. Completion criteria\n   874\t\n   875\tStructure:\n   876\t\n   877\t1. One `fetch` and one `step` serve all four formats with no\n   878\t   format-specific branching; a fifth format is one record.\n   879\t2. No global loader, registry, callback, or cache; every input is an\n   880\t   argument or VM-state value.\n   881\t3. Tri-host parity (JVM, Node, ClojureDart), 0 kondo errors, clean\n   882\t   cljstyle.\n   883\t4. This file and `yin.vm.linker` are pure ASCII with every line at most\n   884\t   80 columns.\n   885\t\n   886\tVerification:\n   887\t\n   888\t5. Every B6 completion criterion (section 11 there) holds for all four\n   889\t   formats where applicable, through both `fetch` and `step`.\n   890\t6. A payload whose address is valid but whose identity is not the one\n   891\t   requested is refused for every format, including the two whose\n   892\t   identity equals the address.\n   893\t7. A request naming a contract the format record does not implement is\n   894\t   `:contract-mismatch` before validation runs.\n   895\t\n   896\tRequire:\n   897\t\n   898\t8. `(require 'foo)` on each of the four backends, over ring buffers,\n   899\t   parks, links, installs, and resumes with `'foo`; the same over the\n   900\t   JVM WebSocket content path.\n   901\t9. The registry value holds no function that arrived by linking; every\n   902\t   linked module's `:bindings` came from an isolated evaluation.\n   903\t10. UCF section 7.4.1 and 7.4.3 carry the `:link` safepoint and pending\n   904\t    variant, and a parked `:link` wait lifts and lowers through UCF's\n   905\t    round-trip test.\n   906\t\n   907\t## 12. Open decisions\n   908\t\n   909\tRecorded so a later plan does not rediscover them. None blocks M1 to M3.\n   910\t\n   911\t- **Authority.** Who may assert `[name :yin.module/manifest address]`,\n   912\t  and what a receiver does with two assertions for one name. D6 places\n   913\t  trust and provenance in composition policy; the name environment as\n   914\t  datoms (section 8.2) gives them a place to be facts. The rule is not\n   915\t  written here.\n   916\t- **SCC identity.** B7 hashes a mutually recursive component as one unit\n   917\t  with canonical member ordering. Whether that unit is a manifest of\n   918\t  manifests or a single image per format is undecided; section 7.4\n   919\t  fixes only the response shape.\n   920\t- **Failure policy.** Retry, deadline, and permanent absence for a\n   921\t  `:pending` link are the composition's (D6). Whether `yin.repl` adopts\n   922\t  the `dao.jing.remote` timing options or its own is an M5 decision.\n   923\t- **Storage-derived identities and the encoder change.** When the pinned\n   924\t  canonical encoding lands, `:yin.ast/code` and `:yin.semantic/code`\n   925\t  identities change while H and R do not. UCF accepts this. Whether the\n   926\t  semantic VM should instead adopt a contract-pinned identity is a UCF\n   927\t  question, not a linker one; the linker is indifferent because\n   928\t  `:hash-fn` is the format's.\n   929\t- **Unrecognized outcomes.** `dao.stream.md` OD-1 proposes that a\n   930\t  consumer treat an unrecognized outcome as refused and not retryable.\n   931\t  The stepped core follows that rule once OD-1 is accepted; until then\n   932\t  it classifies unknown content-server answers as `transport-error`, as\n   933\t  `dao.stream.observe/step` does.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
