{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.module\n     2\t  \"Module system for Yin VM v2.\n     3\t\n     4\t   The v1 module system kept two `defonce` atoms and mutated them at load\n     5\t   time. A registry is a value here: an ordinary map carried in VM state and\n     6\t   supplied by the composition that wires the VM.\n     7\t\n     8\t     (-> (empty-registry)\n     9\t         (register-module 'my.lib {'foo (fn [x] x)})\n    10\t         (register-stream-module))\n    11\t\n    12\t   Nothing in this namespace runs at load time, and nothing registers itself.\n    13\t   A composition that wants Yin source to reach `(stream/...)` registers the\n    14\t   stream module explicitly and supplies `:make-stream` beside it.\"\n    15\t  (:require\n    16\t    [clojure.string :as str]))\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t;; =============================================================================\n    20\t;; Registry values\n    21\t;; =============================================================================\n    22\t\n    23\t(defn empty-registry\n    24\t  \"An empty module registry value.\"\n    25\t  []\n    26\t  {:modules {}, :effect-handlers {}})\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(defn- symbol->path\n    30\t  \"Split a dotted symbol into a get-in path of symbols.\n    31\t   'yin.io.file-input-stream → ['yin 'io 'file-input-stream]\"\n    32\t  [sym]\n    33\t  (mapv symbol (str/split (str sym) #\"\\.\")))\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn register-module\n    37\t  \"Return registry with bindings merged into module-name.\n    38\t   module-name is a dotted symbol; bindings is a map of symbol -> function.\"\n    39\t  [registry module-name bindings]\n    40\t  (update-in (or registry (empty-registry))\n    41\t             (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n    42\t             merge\n    43\t             bindings))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn resolve-module\n    47\t  \"Get a value from a registry value by dotted symbol path.\n    48\t   (resolve-module r 'io)                    → full 'io bindings map\n    49\t   (resolve-module r 'io.file-output-stream) → the specific binding\"\n    50\t  [registry sym]\n    51\t  (get-in (:modules registry) (symbol->path sym)))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn register-effect-handler\n    55\t  \"Return registry with handler-fn installed for effect keyword kw.\n    56\t   Handler: (fn [state effect opts] -> {:state s :value v :blocked? bool})\"\n    57\t  [registry kw handler-fn]\n    58\t  (assoc-in (or registry (empty-registry)) [:effect-handlers kw] handler-fn))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn get-effect-handler\n    62\t  \"Get the handler function for an effect keyword.\"\n    63\t  [registry kw]\n    64\t  (get (:effect-handlers registry) kw))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn list-modules\n    68\t  \"List the top-level module names in a registry value.\"\n    69\t  [registry]\n    70\t  (keys (:modules registry)))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t;; =============================================================================\n    74\t;; Effect descriptors\n    75\t;; =============================================================================\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn effect?\n    78\t  \"Check if a value is an effect descriptor.\"\n    79\t  [x]\n    80\t  (and (map? x) (contains? x :effect)))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn make-effect\n    84\t  \"Create an effect descriptor.\"\n    85\t  [effect-type & {:as params}]\n    86\t  (assoc params :effect effect-type))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t;; =============================================================================\n    90\t;; The `stream` module\n    91\t;; =============================================================================\n    92\t;;\n    93\t;; These are pure data constructors. They touch no stream: Yin source calls\n    94\t;; them through the module system, they return effect maps, and the engine\n    95\t;; interprets those. `take!` is deliberately absent — destructive read is one\n    96\t;; reader's progress and every other reader's data loss, and a v2 `take!` would\n    97\t;; need the reader-position-in-the-medium the contract retired.\n    98\t\n    99\t(defn make\n   100\t  ([] (make nil))\n   101\t  ([cap] {:effect :stream/make, :capacity cap}))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn put!\n   105\t  [s v]\n   106\t  {:effect :stream/put, :stream s, :val v})\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(defn cursor\n   110\t  [s]\n   111\t  {:effect :stream/cursor, :stream s})\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(defn next!\n   115\t  [c]\n   116\t  {:effect :stream/next, :cursor c})\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn close!\n   120\t  [s]\n   121\t  {:effect :stream/close, :stream s})\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\t(def stream-module\n   125\t  \"The v2 `stream` module definition. Registering it is a composition step.\"\n   126\t  {'make make, 'put! put!, 'cursor cursor, 'next! next!, 'close! close!})\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t(defn register-stream-module\n   130\t  \"Return registry with the v2 `stream` module registered.\n   131\t   A composition that calls this must also supply `:make-stream`, or\n   132\t   `(stream/make)` is unsupported and says so.\"\n   133\t  [registry]\n   134\t  (register-module registry 'stream stream-module))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; Built-in effect handlers\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn require-handler\n   142\t  \"Resolve `:module/require` against the registry value only.\n   143\t\n   144\t   v1's clj branch called `clojure.core/require` from inside effect dispatch —\n   145\t   a host call in the middle of interpretation. It does not survive: a module\n   146\t   is either in the registry the composition supplied or it is not.\"\n   147\t  [state effect _opts]\n   148\t  (let [module-name (:module effect)]\n   149\t    (if (some? (resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\n   150\t      {:value module-name, :state state, :blocked? false}\n   151\t      (throw (ex-info \"Module is not in this VM's registry\"\n   152\t                      {:module module-name,\n   153\t                       :available (vec (list-modules (:modules state)))})))))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn default-registry\n   157\t  \"A registry with the built-in effect handlers and no modules.\"\n   158\t  []\n   159\t  (-> (empty-registry)\n   160\t      (register-effect-handler :module/require require-handler)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
