{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '330,495p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | nl -ba -v 330\nsed -n '496,590p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | nl -ba -v 496\"","aggregated_output":"   330\t            (waitset/check {:waiting wait-set} waitset-resolver (:store state))\n   331\t            v (assoc state\n   332\t                     :store store\n   333\t                     :wait-set (:waiting (:waitset result)))]\n   334\t        (update v\n   335\t                :ready-queue (fnil into [])\n   336\t                (make-woken-run-queue-entries v woken))))))\n   337\t\n   338\t\n   339\t(declare handle-effect resume-continuation)\n   340\t\n   341\t\n   342\t(defn run-loop\n   343\t  \"Generic eval loop with scheduler support. Ready entries are pure data;\n   344\t   `resume-fn` pops and restores them.\"\n   345\t  [state active? step-fn resume-fn]\n   346\t  (loop [v state]\n   347\t    (let [q (or (:ready-queue v) [])]\n   348\t      (cond (active? v) (recur (step-fn v))\n   349\t            (:blocked? v) (let [v' (check-wait-set v)]\n   350\t                            (if-let [resumed (resume-fn v')]\n   351\t                              (recur resumed)\n   352\t                              (telemetry/emit-snapshot v' :blocked)))\n   353\t            (seq q) (if-let [resumed (resume-fn v)]\n   354\t                      (recur resumed)\n   355\t                      v)\n   356\t            :else (if (:halted? v) (telemetry/emit-snapshot v :halt) v)))))\n   357\t\n   358\t\n   359\t(def ^:private waitset-diagnostics\n   360\t  \"The statuses `dao.stream.waitset/check` wakes an entry it could not poll\n   361\t   at all with: an unsupported reason, an unresolvable entry, or an answer —\n   362\t   or transport — it could not interpret. No park site in `yin.vm` produces\n   363\t   an entry that earns one, and an entry that earns one must not reach a\n   364\t   restore function as a value.\"\n   365\t  #{:dao.stream.waitset/unsupported-reason\n   366\t    :dao.stream.waitset/unresolved\n   367\t    :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer})\n   368\t\n   369\t\n   370\t(defn- terminal-resume-outcome\n   371\t  \"The outcome a woken entry resolved with, when it is one the immediate\n   372\t   path raises as an error. `handle-put` and `handle-next` throw for every\n   373\t   outcome outside ok/end/gap, and whether the first attempt blocked must not\n   374\t   change that. A waitset diagnostic is terminal whatever the entry's\n   375\t   `:reason` — an unsupported reason is by definition outside the\n   376\t   `#{:next :put}` this check otherwise reads — so it is named here rather\n   377\t   than falling through to the restore. An entry that was never polled\n   378\t   carries no status.\"\n   379\t  [entry]\n   380\t  (let [status (:status entry)]\n   381\t    (cond\n   382\t      (contains? waitset-diagnostics status) status\n   383\t      (contains? #{:next :put} (:reason entry))\n   384\t      (when-not (contains? #{nil :ok :end :dao.stream/gap} status) status))))\n   385\t\n   386\t\n   387\t(defn- throw-terminal-resume!\n   388\t  \"Fail a resumed entry exactly as the immediate operation would have. A\n   389\t   waitset diagnostic names its status and the entry that earned it: there\n   390\t   is no stream operation whose error vocabulary it belongs to.\"\n   391\t  [entry o]\n   392\t  (cond\n   393\t    (contains? waitset-diagnostics o)\n   394\t    (fail \"Wait-set entry woke with a diagnostic\" {:status o, :entry entry})\n   395\t    (= :next (:reason entry))\n   396\t    (fail \"Stream read failed\"\n   397\t          {:outcome o,\n   398\t           :stream-id (:stream-id entry),\n   399\t           :cursor-id (:id (:cursor-ref entry))})\n   400\t    :else (fail \"Stream append failed\"\n   401\t                {:outcome o, :stream-id (:stream-id entry)})))\n   402\t\n   403\t\n   404\t(defn resume-from-run-queue\n   405\t  \"Pop first entry from the ready-queue, merge store-updates, and restore\n   406\t   VM-specific context.\n   407\t\n   408\t   Restoration is dispatched here rather than carried on the entry, so a\n   409\t   ready entry holds registers, ids, and values — never a closure. The\n   410\t   terminal-outcome check runs before the restore: a woken retry that ended\n   411\t   in an outcome the immediate operation raises as an error must fail the\n   412\t   same way here, not reach Yin code as a value.\n   413\t\n   414\t   `restore-fn` is called with three arguments, `base entry val`, where\n   415\t   `val` is the woken `:value` — the same signature `resume-continuation`\n   416\t   uses, so one restore serves both engine call sites\n   417\t   (`yin.vm.engine.md` §7, edit 2).\"\n   418\t  [state restore-fn]\n   419\t  (let [run-queue (or (:ready-queue state) [])]\n   420\t    (when (seq run-queue)\n   421\t      (let [entry (first run-queue)\n   422\t            rest-queue (subvec run-queue 1)\n   423\t            base (assoc state\n   424\t                        :ready-queue rest-queue\n   425\t                        :store (merge (:store state) (:store-updates entry))\n   426\t                        :blocked? false\n   427\t                        :halted? false)]\n   428\t        (if-let [terminal (terminal-resume-outcome entry)]\n   429\t          (throw-terminal-resume! entry terminal)\n   430\t          (restore-fn base entry (:value entry)))))))\n   431\t\n   432\t\n   433\t(defn scheduler-round\n   434\t  \"One round between continuations: poll the wait set, then resume whatever\n   435\t   woke, through `restore-fn` (`base entry val -> state`, the one restore\n   436\t   signature `yin.vm.engine.md` §2.1 states). Returns the polled state when\n   437\t   nothing woke, so a caller always gets a state back.\n   438\t\n   439\t   This is `yin.vm.semantic/scheduler-round` with its restore made a\n   440\t   parameter (`yin.vm.engine.md` §7, edit 1); every VM was writing this\n   441\t   composition by hand.\"\n   442\t  [state restore-fn]\n   443\t  (let [v' (check-wait-set state)]\n   444\t    (or (resume-from-run-queue v' restore-fn) v')))\n   445\t\n   446\t\n   447\t(defn park-continuation\n   448\t  \"Add a parked continuation entry and halt the VM.\"\n   449\t  [state cont-fields]\n   450\t  (let [id-counter (or (:id-counter state) 0)\n   451\t        park-id (keyword (str \"parked-\" id-counter))\n   452\t        parked (merge {:type :parked-continuation, :id park-id} cont-fields)]\n   453\t    (-> state\n   454\t        (update :parked assoc park-id parked)\n   455\t        (assoc :value parked\n   456\t               :halted? true\n   457\t               :id-counter (inc id-counter))\n   458\t        (telemetry/emit-snapshot :park {:parked-id park-id}))))\n   459\t\n   460\t\n   461\t(defn resume-continuation\n   462\t  \"Restore state from a parked continuation.\"\n   463\t  [state parked-id resume-val restore-fn]\n   464\t  (if-let [parked (get-in state [:parked parked-id])]\n   465\t    (let [new-state (update state :parked dissoc parked-id)]\n   466\t      (-> (restore-fn new-state parked resume-val)\n   467\t          (telemetry/emit-snapshot :resume {:parked-id parked-id})))\n   468\t    (fail \"Cannot resume: parked continuation not found\"\n   469\t          {:parked-id parked-id})))\n   470\t\n   471\t\n   472\t(defn gensym\n   473\t  \"Generate a unique ID and return [id updated-state].\"\n   474\t  ([state] (gensym state \"id\"))\n   475\t  ([state prefix]\n   476\t   (let [id-counter (or (:id-counter state) 0)\n   477\t         id (gen-id prefix id-counter)]\n   478\t     [id (assoc state :id-counter (inc id-counter))])))\n   479\t\n   480\t\n   481\t(defn handle-stream-block\n   482\t  [result entry]\n   483\t  (if (:park result)\n   484\t    (let [entry (or entry\n   485\t                    (fail \"Parked entry required for blocking stream\"\n   486\t                          {:result result}))\n   487\t          new-state (-> (:state result)\n   488\t                        (update :wait-set (fnil conj []) entry)\n   489\t                        (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n   490\t                               :blocked? true\n   491\t                               :halted? false))]\n   492\t      {:state new-state, :value :yin/blocked, :blocked? true})\n   493\t    {:state (:state result), :value (:value result), :blocked? false}))\n   494\t\n   495\t\n   496\t(defn handle-effect\n   497\t  \"Dispatch an effect and return {:state updated-state :value v :blocked? bool}.\n   498\t   park-entry-fns maps :stream/put and :stream/next to functions that build\n   499\t   wait entries.\n   500\t\n   501\t   A parked entry is stored as the builder left it plus, for a writer, the\n   502\t   `:datom` it retries: registers and resource ids only. Neither the live\n   503\t   stream handle nor a restore closure is attached — `check-wait-set`\n   504\t   resolves handles from the store at every poll, and the scheduler that pops\n   505\t   a woken entry dispatches restoration itself — so a blocked entry is pure\n   506\t   data and survives serialization.\"\n   507\t  [state effect {:keys [park-entry-fns], :as opts}]\n   508\t  (let [park-entry (get park-entry-fns (:effect effect))\n   509\t        result\n   510\t        (case (:effect effect)\n   511\t          :vm/store-put {:state (assoc state\n   512\t                                       :store (assoc (:store state)\n   513\t                                                     (:key effect)\n   514\t                                                     (:val effect))),\n   515\t                         :value (:val effect),\n   516\t                         :blocked? false}\n   517\t          :stream/make\n   518\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"stream\")\n   519\t                [stream-ref new-state] (handle-make s' effect id)]\n   520\t            {:state new-state, :value stream-ref, :blocked? false})\n   521\t          :stream/cursor\n   522\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"cursor\")\n   523\t                [cursor-ref new-state] (handle-cursor s' effect id)]\n   524\t            {:state new-state, :value cursor-ref, :blocked? false})\n   525\t          :stream/put\n   526\t          (let [result (handle-put state effect)]\n   527\t            (if (:park result)\n   528\t              (let [built-entry (when park-entry\n   529\t                                  (park-entry state effect result))\n   530\t                    built-entry (if (and built-entry (not (:datom built-entry)))\n   531\t                                  (assoc built-entry :datom (:val effect))\n   532\t                                  built-entry)]\n   533\t                (handle-stream-block result built-entry))\n   534\t              {:state (:state result),\n   535\t               :value (:value result),\n   536\t               :blocked? false}))\n   537\t          :stream/next\n   538\t          (let [result (handle-next state effect)]\n   539\t            (if (:park result)\n   540\t              (let [built-entry (when park-entry\n   541\t                                  (park-entry state effect result))]\n   542\t                (handle-stream-block result built-entry))\n   543\t              {:state (:state result),\n   544\t               :value (:value result),\n   545\t               :blocked? false}))\n   546\t          :stream/close\n   547\t          (let [close-result (handle-close state effect)]\n   548\t            {:state (:state close-result), :value nil, :blocked? false})\n   549\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"effect\")\n   550\t                handler (module/get-effect-handler (:modules state)\n   551\t                                                   (:effect effect))]\n   552\t            (if handler\n   553\t              (handler s' effect (assoc opts :id id))\n   554\t              (fail \"Unknown effect\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\n   555\t    (update result\n   556\t            :state\n   557\t            (fn [result-state]\n   558\t              (telemetry/emit-snapshot (assoc result-state\n   559\t                                              :value (:value result))\n   560\t                                       :effect\n   561\t                                       {:effect-type (:effect effect)})))))\n   562\t\n   563\t\n   564\t;; =============================================================================\n   565\t;; Program Cache Machinery\n   566\t;; =============================================================================\n   567\t\n   568\t(def default-compiled-cache-limit 8)\n   569\t\n   570\t\n   571\t(defn build-program-index\n   572\t  [datoms]\n   573\t  (group-by first (vec datoms)))\n   574\t\n   575\t\n   576\t(defn frame-versions\n   577\t  [frame]\n   578\t  (loop [f frame\n   579\t         acc #{}]\n   580\t    (if (map? f)\n   581\t      (let [acc (cond-> acc (:compiled-version f) (conj (:compiled-version f)))]\n   582\t        (recur (:next f) acc))\n   583\t      acc)))\n   584\t\n   585\t\n   586\t(defn collect-frame-versions\n   587\t  [frames]\n   588\t  (reduce (fn [acc f] (into acc (frame-versions f))) #{} (or frames [])))\n   589\t\n   590\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
